{
  "comment": [
    "The fake library for the documentation screenshots. Read by library.py, which writes",
    "one song folder per entry into the scratch data directory. Nothing here is downloaded",
    "and no lyrics are stored: a folder is a header-only USDX txt, a generated cover and,",
    "where 'video' is true, a placeholder video file.",
    "",
    "'usdb_id' is what makes a song id stable across seed runs: library.py writes it into",
    "wingman.json, so the scanner mints 'usdb:<usdb_id>' instead of a random local id.",
    "Keep the ids unique and keep them out of the range fake_usdb.py serves (9001 and up).",
    "",
    "Four entries are fixed and must not be renamed. The documentation guidelines name",
    "them: Sandstorm (1101), Tequila (1102), Rap God (1103) and the duet I Got You Babe",
    "(1104). At least ten entries have a year between 1980 and 1989, which is what the",
    "worked achievement example in the docs counts."
  ],
